# as a family first"). Three definitions in draco.drake, authored DRAKE-FIRST and the JSON written by the
# compiled parser:
#   Presence(T)                    modules [Present, Absent]                 (root; rooted to DracoType)
#   Present(T) from Presence(T)    elements fix value T; factory par value T, body fix value T _value
#   Absent(T)  from Presence(T)    factory (bare)
#   Drake.drake                    types [Presence Present Absent]           (the runtime domain lists them)
#
# THE FIRST PARAMETERIZED SEALED FAMILY the generator emits, which is exactly what this step was for. Run
# against the compiled engine (classes + an OVERLAY of src/main/resources, so the derivation chain finds
# Presence.json rather than a stub), the family came out with three defects, two of them the engine's:
#   1. the root's discriminated codec named a `T` no object can name (`as[T]`, `x.value.asJson`), and the
#      members' Codec.sub named `Presence` without its argument. FIX (engine): a parameterized family has
#      NO host codec — codecDeclaration returns "" for a root with type parameters and for a member whose
#      discriminated parent has them — the rule a parameterized plain type (Value(F)) already lives by.
#      Presence's codec is the CODEC ASPECT's business, written in drake (agreement item 8); until then the
#      family is constructible, comparable and projectable, not serializable. No circe import remains.
#   2. Present's Null was `apply[Nothing](_value = null.asInstanceOf[T])` — T out of scope, and a null cast
#      to Nothing throws on first touch. FIX (engine): when any factory parameter is typed by one of the
#      type's own variables (typeVariable: the bound leaf's first operand), Null instantiates at ANY —
#      `apply[Any](_value = null.asInstanceOf[Any])`. Every existing Null is at Nothing and none mentions
#      a variable, so no committed line moves.
#   3. the member companions lacked `with DracoType` / `override` — NOT an engine defect: the compiled
#      classes' resources had no Presence.json, so chainHits met a typeName-only stub. The overlay fixed
#      the run; nothing to change.
