--- MESSAGE ---
Presence, Present and Absent are the first members of draco.drake

draco's own option, authored drake-first: `Presence(T)` with `modules [Present, Absent]`, `Present(T)`
carrying `par value T`, `Absent(T)` bare and parameterized, because variance is a later concept. The
runtime domain lists them. It is the first parameterized sealed family the generator emits, and the
generator learned two things from it: a parameterized family carries no host codec, since a
discriminated union over `Presence[T]` cannot name an `Encoder[T]` and the family's codec is the codec
aspect's business in drake; and a `Null` whose factory parameter is typed by the type's own variable
instantiates at `Any`, since `Nothing` has no value to pass. DracoGenTest gates the family as one file,
as it gates TypeElement's.

Next, as agreed: `fold` as a dyn on Presence defined by dispatch in Present and Absent; then
lazy-by-default with `now`; then `ifThenElse` as the second dyn.

